-- title:
--   Minimal primes over q in the pole chart are the centres of W₀,W₁
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and write $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((t))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $N_0q$. Let $W:\mathrm{Fin}\,2\to$ valuation subrings of $F$ satisfy: (i) $f\in W_0$ exactly when $f\cdot y=x$ in $F$-expansions for some Laurent series $x,y$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo $q$ is nonzero; (ii) $f\in W_1$ exactly when `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N₀ q f` $\in W_0$, where that map is a chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ with the property `IsAtkinLehnerAutFull N₀ q` (the identity if none exists); (iii) $W_0\neq W_1$; (iv) for each $i$, the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $W_i$, every $P(j)$ with $P\in\mathbb{Z}[X]$ nonzero modulo $q$ is a unit of $W_i$ (here $j$ is `jq`, viewed in $F$), and every nonunit of $W_i$ becomes an element of $W_i$ after multiplication by $q^{-1}$; (v) any valuation subring of $F$ with the two properties in (iv) equals $W_0$ or $W_1$. Then every element of the chart subalgebra `IgusaScheme.chartAlgInf (N₀ * q) q` of $F$ over the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals with denominator prime to $q$ — namely `chartAlg` at the singleton $\{(\mathtt{jFull}\,(N_0q))^{-1}\}$ — lies in both $W_0$ and $W_1$; and there are ideals $P_0,P_1$ of that subalgebra with $a\in P_i$ iff $a$ is a nonunit of $W_i$, each $P_i$ prime, $P_0\neq P_1$, and the minimal primes of the ideal generated by $q$ being exactly $\{P_0,P_1\}$.
--
--   This is the pole-chart counterpart of the corresponding statement for the finite chart: it identifies the two primes of the Igusa pole-chart ring minimal over $q$ with the centres of the two valuation rings of the modular function field above $q$, reflecting the two components of the fibre at $q$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$. It is used in the analysis of the reduction of the level-$N_0q$ model package at $q$ and in the comparison of the two charts of the Igusa scheme.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel_exists_minimalPrimes_chartAlgInf_span_eq_pair_of_valuationSubring_pair.lean

